    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0427" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg385"/>

                <head>Mr. Hyland to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 80.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States of
                                America,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bermuda,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-07-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 25, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you that the
                    British brig Eagle, Captain Norfolk, sailed from this port on the 22d instant
                    for Liverpool, Great Britain, with a cargo of cotton, taken from warehouse here,
                    and a large portion of bar silver from the rebel steamship Florida, the whole
                    valued at £50,000. The silver has been transferred by bill of sale to John J.
                    Bourne, the agent of the rebel States.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, with much respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. C. J. HYLAND, <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Vice-Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
